title: The fork's own children are left, in no note, and the save does not warn of them.
pid: ca802dbb-403d-4b28-8f73-e8621db48a61
body: |2-
  Deleting any node in skg leaves its children; nothing cascades. So a
  reply typed under the fork outlives it, findable only by search.
  The recursive delete ('C-u C-c <backspace>') cannot take it with the
  fork when the fork holds the message's own children: those are
  foreign, and the save refuses to delete them. The other way: delete
  with a fork the owned children that no other note contains, so the
  one gesture takes the reply too. That would give 'delete' a meaning
  it has nowhere else; it is the question I would ask Jeff.
